WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.317
Modern organizations generate enormous amounts of security-relevant information.

00:00:03.317 --> 00:00:06.936
Firewalls, servers, cloud platforms, endpoint tools, identity providers, applications,

00:00:06.936 --> 00:00:09.349
and network devices all produce logs.

00:00:09.349 --> 00:00:12.566
Each source can tell part of the story,

00:00:12.566 --> 00:00:16.185
but none of them gives complete visibility by itself.

00:00:16.185 --> 00:00:19.000
Reviewing these logs manually is nearly impossible.

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:23.423
Important warning signs may be buried among millions of normal events.

00:00:23.423 --> 00:00:26.238
A suspicious login, firewall deny, endpoint alert,

00:00:26.238 --> 00:00:31.868
and cloud configuration change may matter more when viewed together than when reviewed separately.

00:00:31.868 --> 00:00:34.281
SIEM platforms help organizations collect, organize,

00:00:34.281 --> 00:00:39.508
and analyze this information so security teams can identify suspicious activity more effectively.

00:00:39.508 --> 00:00:45.540
SIEM exists because defenders need visibility across many systems rather than isolated pieces of information.
